Language English

Book OpenGate Ordered No Keep Looped
	Triggered By @InteractAltar

	Mark Step3Repeat Read

    Page Step1Prolog
        Text """
			Matthias stands at the altar, arms raised, speaking in a language
			you do not understand. Spread before him are the tools and materials
			required for the ritual.

			The boy is chained to the floor, crying and quietly begging his
			father to stop. Nearby, a woman cowers on the floor, shackled to the altar.

			Matthias continues the incantation, but this time the waves of power
			do not radiate from him — they pour from the air itself, rushing
			into him.
			
            If you have the {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the
			{c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the {c:QItemElderSign}, you can
			begin to disrupt the ritual.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this task and only
            while standing at the altar in the same space as Matthias.
        
            Are you ready?
        """

		If firstRitual >= firstRitualWoman Then Text """
			Matthias stands at the altar, arms raised, speaking in a language
			you do not understand. Spread before him are the tools and materials
			required for the ritual.

			The boy is chained to the floor, crying and quietly begging his
			father to stop. At Matthias's feet lies a dead woman, her face
			frozen in a scream that will never fade.
			
            If you have the {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the
			{c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the {c:QItemElderSign}, you can
			begin to disrupt the ritual.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this task and only
            while standing at the altar in the same space as Matthias.
        
            Are you ready?
        """

        Button 1 "Speak the words"
		Button 2 "Not Yet"

		If selection = 1 And firstRitual >= firstRitualWoman Then Goto Step1
		If selection = 1 Then Goto Woman
		Exit
	End Page Step1Prolog
	
	Page Woman
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenDeadWoman
		
		Text """
			As you step closer, Matthias lowers his arms, then flings them
			skyward.

			The woman screams, gasps for air, then screams again. The power you
			felt before comes in waves, but this time it feels as though it is flowing into Matthias.

			Something indescribable happens to the woman's body and she stops screaming. She goes rigid, then limp.

			A brief glow surrounds Matthias. He lowers one arm just long enough
			to flip to another page in the book resting on the altar.

			The woman is dead.

			Sarah whispers, <<Matthias has recharged himself. He is at the final
			stage. He is ready to open the gate.>>
		"""
		
		Remove TokenLiveWoman
		
		Goto Step1
	End Page Woman
	
	Page step1
		firstRitual = 0
		mainRitual = mainRitualStarted
		
        Text """
			You look more closely at the altar.

			You notice that Matthias does not possess an {c:QItemElderSign}.
			That means he will need blood to keep the gate open. You must stop
			him before he uses you to supply it.

			You think back to the counter-spell you memorized earlier. Raising
			the {c:QItemRitualKnife} and the chalice above your head, you speak
			the words.

			Matthias's head snaps toward you, as though he is seeing you for
			the first time. Your eyes lock, and you see a look that is both
			determined and haunted.

			He turns back to the altar to continue.

			No sound comes out of his mouth.

			Slowly, he looks back at you.
			
			This step is complete.
        """
    End Page Step1

    Page Step2
        Prolog """
			Your cousin lowers his gaze to the dagger in his hand. Though no
			sound escapes him, you can see his lips moving.
        """

        Button "Stab Matthias first"

        Text """
			You choose your moment and lunge at him with your knife. He deftly
			sidesteps, and your blade glances off his robe, doing no harm.

			You think you can pivot and strike more cleanly. Test {agility}.

			For each Unique Item you possess, you may roll one additional die.
        """
		
		// even if we pass, we fail
        Test Quota 10 Set passWhoCares
    End Page Step2

    Page Step3
        Prolog """
			He steps away again, and you stumble forward, colliding with him
			and knocking the {c:QItemRitualDagger} from his grasp. It clatters
			across the altar as you regain your footing and step back.
        """

		Button "Speak the words"

        Text """
			Matthias snatches up the knife and begins the incantation again, his
			voice once again booming with power. The blade suddenly flares with light, then
			settles into a steady, pulsing glow.
			
			You speak the words again. Test {will}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        """

        // even if we pass, we fail
		Test Quota 4 Set passWhoCares
    End Page Step3

    Page Step3Fail
        Text """
			You fumble the words... and nothing happens.

			Matthias ignores you and draws the blade across his palm.
        
            Suffer 2 Horror ({will} negates).
			
			<<You must stop him,>> Sarah stammers.
        """

        Mark Step3Repeat Unread
    End Page Step3Fail

	Page Step3Repeat
		Prolog """
			Surprised that your spell failed, you raise your arms again.
		"""
		
		Button "Speak the words"
		
		Text """
			You begin speaking, hoping to silence him again. Test {will}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
		"""

		Test Quota 4 Set passOpenGateStep3
		If passOpenGateStep3 Then Goto Step4
	End Page Step3Repeat

	Page Step3RepeatFail
	
		Text """
			Matthias seems unfazed as blood wells from the cut in his palm. You
			glance at the dagger and chalice raised in your hands, wondering
			why nothing is happening.

			You draw a steadying breath, determined to stop this madness.
		"""

		Mark Unread
		Mark Step3Repeat Unread
	End Page Step3RepeatFail

    Page Step4
		Mark Step3RepeatFail Read
		
        Prolog """
			Matthias squeezes blood from his fist into the chalice, speaking in
			that same unknown language.

			As he does, you feel your spell take hold... and his voice falters,
			then vanishes once more.
        """

        Button "Make your move"

        Text """
			With Matthias frustrated and distracted, you lunge for the skull.
			If only you can reach it before he... does something.
			
			Test {agility}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
       """
   
       // even if we pass, we fail
	   Test Quota 10 Set passWhoCares
    End Page Step4

	Page Step4Fail
		Text """
			Matthias lashes out, his dagger flashing in the low light. The blade
			catches your arm, forcing you to drop your weapon.

			Drop {c:QItemRitualKnife}. Take 2 {damage} ({agility} negates).

			Matthias squeezes more blood into the chalice. As it fills, the
			vessel begins to change in a way you cannot fully describe. It
			thrums with power now, resonant and dangerous, much like the dagger
			in his hand.
		"""
	End Page Step4Fail
	
    Page KillHim
		Prolog """
			You hesitate for a moment, forcing yourself to think. You need to 
			decide what to do next---and you need to decide quickly.

			Sarah quavers, <<You have to do something. He's nearly finished
			casting. Please.>>
		"""
		Button "Make your decision"
		
        Text """
			The futility of trying to stop your uncle from completing the ritual
			sinks in. There is only one way to end this. You're going to have to
			kill him.

			Across the room, your friends fight for their lives against what
			feels like a never-ending stream of townsfolk clad in cult robes.

			Your cousin remains focused on his casting, oblivious to everything
			else.
        """
	
		// we need to replace unattackable monster with one we can attack
		
		Call Event SpawnAltarMatthiasOpenGate
		
		// does this make the DVM go away? (??? why?)
		Remove QItemDvm
    End Page KillHim
	
	Epilog
		Not Visible
		
		No Prolog
		No Text
	End Epilog
	
	Page SarahTransports
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @AnotherRequirementCompleted If goal = goalOpenGate And foundKnife And foundDvm And foundElderSign And foundDungeonCell And exploredCryptViaChapel And exploredDungeonCaveViaBasement
		
		Text """
			Sarah smiles for the first time and says out loud, <<That's it! Now
			we know what's happening, where Matthias is working, and what to do about
			it. I think I can take us where we need to be.>>

			She seems to grow taller — and fainter at the same time, her form
			turning translucent.

			Suddenly, the world shifts.

			You are somewhere else. Disoriented.

			There is noise. Light. Someone shouting. People rush past you, their
			forms blurred and indistinct. It all feels distant... unreal.
		"""
		
		If firstRitual < firstRitualWoman Call MythosFirstRitualOpenGate.Woman
		
		firstRitual = false
		Trigger @ExploreAltar
		Goto Init
	End Page SarahTransports
End Book OpenGate

Book MatthiasOpenGateActivation Ordered No Keep
	Triggered By @MatthiasOpenGateActivation
	
	Page First
		Text """
			Matthias lifts the chalice, a single drop of blood sliding down its
			inner surface. He studies it carefully, then, seemingly satisfied,
			sets it back upon the altar.

			Raising his other arm, the dagger still clenched in his hand, he
			steadies the chalice before reaching to turn a page in his book.
			He glances down at the text, then looks to the boy and begins to
			speak.

			As the words leave his mouth, a wave of energy radiates from him,
			and you are briefly stunned.
			
			Each investigator takes 1 facedown damage ({agility} negates).
			
			Each cultist takes 1 damage.
		"""
	End Page First

	Page Second
		Text """
			Matthias begins speaking again, power radiating from him as it did
			before. His focus is fixed on his son as the boy begins to move.

			You watch as he starts to hover, slowly lifted as though suspended
			by an invisible string. The chain clanks as it slips free.

			Sarah panics, her gaze darting back and forth between her uncle and
			her cousin. <<Do something!>> she yells. <<Do something now!>>

			Matthias doesn't notice. All his attention is consumed by the words
			he chants---and by the boy who is their target.
		"""
	End Page Second
	
	Page Third
		Text """
			The boy screams as a glow begins to gather around him. He stops
			rising when the chain binding him to the floor pulls taut, its links
			straining. He is still screaming.

			At the altar, Matthias continues the incantation, utterly focused---
			so intent that everyone in the room can feel it.

			Sarah shrieks at him. <<Stop! Please, stop!>>

			With a final flourish of his knife, Matthias completes the spell.
			A bolt lashes from the blade's tip into the boy's chest. The instant
			it strikes, the screaming stops. The boy goes rigid.

			Everyone turns to watch. For a moment, the room falls completely
			silent.

			Then, with a roar, the boy... changes.

			He becomes something more. Surging. Abyssal. Unstable. The gate is
			open and, somehow, the boy <i>is</i> the gate.

			Sarah cries out in anguish.

			The gate sputters.
		End Text
		
		gateOpen = true
	End Page Third
	
	Page Fourth
		Text """
			The fight is exhausting you. For a moment, you falter and stop to
			catch your breath.

			As you do, Matthias flips through several pages of the book, smiling
			when he finds what he seeks. He raises his arms and begins speaking
			again. His blood still drips from the dagger, spattering on the
			altar. You can feel it in the air with each drop that falls.

			Sarah shouts, <<He's beginning the summoning. The Ancient One has
			heard him. We're running out of time!>>

			Another cultist rushes into the room. He steps toward the gate,
			raises a dagger, mutters words you do not understand, then slits his
			own throat.

			When his blood touches the boy's chain, the gate steadies. It still
			crackles and spits, but the surges are weaker now, less erratic.
		"""
		
		summoning = true
	End Page Fourth
	
	Page Fifth
		Text """
			Matthias continues to chant, his voice booming through the chamber.
			He punctuates each phrase by stabbing the air with his dagger.

			Suddenly, he falls silent, lowers his arms, and simply watches the
			gate as a lone tentacle pushes through.
			
			The investigation is over.
		"""
		
		outcome = gameLose
		Trigger @GameOver
	End Page Fifth
	
End Book MatthiasOpenGateActivation
